Stage dependency headers into an ex_unit_test's ERL_LIBS.

ex_unit_test builds its ERL_LIBS tree with erl_libs_contents but leaves the
`headers` argument commented out, so it defaults to False and a dependency's
include/ directory is never staged. Compilation rules stage headers; tests do
not, and there is no reason for the difference -- Elixir reads a dependency's
public header at RUNTIME whenever a module uses Record.extract/2:

    @span_fields Record.extract(:span, from_lib: "opentelemetry/include/otel_span.hrl")

which resolves through code:lib_dir/1 against ERL_LIBS. Without the headers the
test dies before running a single case:

    ** (RuntimeError) error parsing file .../serviceradar_deps/opentelemetry/include/otel_span.hrl,
       got: {:error, :enoent}

target_info stays commented out: unlike erlang_bytecode, ex_unit_test has no
app of its own to stage, only its deps.

--- a/private/ex_unit_test.bzl
+++ b/private/ex_unit_test.bzl
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
     erl_libs_files = erl_libs_contents(
         ctx,
         # target_info = None,
-        # headers = True,
+        headers = True,
         deps = flat_deps(ctx.attr.deps),
         ez_deps = ctx.files.ez_deps,
         dir = erl_libs_dir,
